From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: OpenWrt <openwrt@openwrt.org>
Subject: [PATCH] arm64: dts: rockchip: use LubanCat 2 V2/V3 RGMII delays

The upstream device tree carries the RGMII delays of the original board
(tx 0x22 / rx 0x0e and tx 0x21 / rx 0x0e). The vendor tree revised the
trace compensation starting with revision V2 and uses tx 0x25 / rx 0x01
on both MACs for V2 and V3, so apply those here.

Drop this patch if the target board is a V1.

--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/rockchip/rk3568-lubancat-2.dts
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/rockchip/rk3568-lubancat-2.dts
@@ -479,8 +479,8 @@
 		     &gmac0_rgmii_clk
 		     &gmac0_rgmii_bus>;
 
-	tx_delay = <0x22>;
-	rx_delay = <0x0e>;
+	tx_delay = <0x25>;
+	rx_delay = <0x01>;
 
 	phy-handle = <&rgmii_phy0>;
 	status = "okay";
@@ -512,8 +512,8 @@
 		     &gmac1m1_rgmii_clk
 		     &gmac1m1_rgmii_bus>;
 
-	tx_delay = <0x21>;
-	rx_delay = <0x0e>;
+	tx_delay = <0x25>;
+	rx_delay = <0x01>;
 
 	phy-handle = <&rgmii_phy1>;
 	status = "okay";
